A bit off topic but interesting anyway - Do you have Windows 2000 running on
you PWS500a?  I would be interested in information about that.  Send me a
message off of this list at cdtaylor51@hotmail.com if you would please.

As for the problems with the CDrom drives.  I think that it is pretty
commonly accepted that the drives that run at 8X or less have problems with
CDs produced on faster drives.  That's because up until the 8X drives they
all spun the disks at pretty much fixed speeds.  Then the newer drives went
to the variable speed - I have heard that some drives will now spin at
speeds up to 12000 rpm.  I have an old DEC RRD45 SCSI CDrom in my PWS600a/au
machine now and it has read everything I have put into it.  However, I have
not been able to boot from the Mandrake 7.1 CD that I made.  I have a Redhat
7.1 disk that boots but it doesn't like my video card (PowerStrom 4D20) and
I reluctant to change the card as it works with NT, VMS and Tru64 Unix.  I
am looking for a version of Linux that will work with my video card.   Any
ideas or suggestions would be appreciated.

TIA

Chuck Taylor




