> 
> I have a Redhat 7.1 disk that boots but it doesn't like my video
> card (PowerStrom 4D20) and I reluctant to change the card as it
> works with NT, VMS and Tru64 Unix.  I am looking for a version of
> Linux that will work with my video card.  Any ideas or suggestions
> would be appreciated.

Hmm; 4D20 is 24-plane TGA2, I believe, and I'm pretty sure that RH 7.1
had patches in there (4.0.3) for that (though they are better in 4.1.0
and 4.2.0).

What problems do you see?

Did you put a BusID option in the Device section, as sometimes that's
necessary?

Hopefully, it got configured as a TGA during installation (I don't
remember if the XFree86 or RH X configurators recognize it as a TGA2).
Or it might have been detected as a Cirrus, as there is a low-end
Cirrus VGA chip on there to provide text console only.

--Jay++

