On Thu, Feb 28, 2002 at 02:02:59PM -0600, Denison, Javier wrote:
>
> Anybody experience the system locking up during the load of linux on alpha?.
> I am trying to load redhat 7.1 but have experienced similar problems in the
> past with Debian on NTSI 500mhz. The current load I am trying hangs during
> the lad of desktop utilities modules. not 100% sure on name . Trying
> different load methods I get different results, using 0 with 2.4
> installation gives me the most trouble.

Not sure what the NTSI-500 is, but AS500, with its builtin QLogic SCSI
controller, often is problematic with any 2.4.x kernels that use the
stock Linux QLogic driver (qlogcisp.c). RH 7.1 uses a 2.4.3 kernel base,
while RH 7.0 and earlier used a 2.2.x based one, where the problem, for
some reason, is not often encountered.

The configuration giving it the most trouble is a single SCSI bus
cable connecting HDDs and CDROM to the onboard QLogic controller. Tape
units have also been know to cause problems.

Solutions (assuming you want to use the CD to do the install):

1. get the CDROM off the SCSI cable that has the HDDs, preferably onto
   a separate controller (NCR is fine, another QLogic is OK as well, but
   Adaptec is not supported by the SRM console, and there's no IDE
   pinout).

2. do a network-based install, ie don't depend on the CD.

Once you've got the install, you can build a custom kernel with a
different QLogic driver, from www.feral.com (thanks, Matt), that
is known to work much better in almost all cases. Then you can put
the CD back onto the QLogic SCSI bus with the HDDs.

Good luck.

--Jay++

