Success!!!

I have installed RedHat 7.1 on my PWS600a/au.  I had a few problems.  First,
the CD that I was trying to install from had a scratch on it.  Second, the
installer didn't like my video card but I was able to go through the lores
install and select the TGA +3D option and it worked just fine.  Thirdly, and
the annoying thing is that the installer didn't tell me that the disk drive
that I was trying to install on already had a Windows disklabel on it and my
system kept crashing.  Once I got that figured out everything worked just
fine.  It seems that the installer should be little bit smarter - at least
it could print out some sort of error message that sends you in the right
direction.

Now that I have RedHat 7.1 installed on my system - I am a newbie to Linux -
and I am pretty impressed with what I have seen thus far.  I even got to
observe a power-loss crash of my system due to an unexpected  power
interruption.  Very impressive that the system verifies and fixes any
corruption that has happened in the file system.

I now have:
    RedHat Linux 7.1 on one disk
    Windows NT 4.0 on a second disk
    Tru64 5.1a on a third disk
    OpenVMS 7.3 on a fourth disk

I am a pretty happy camper right now.  I am now looking for training on
Linux.  I have already found some things but I am open to suggestions.

Thanks for your help and suggestions.

Chuck
