The following suggestion may be too late, and it only addresses
the issue of where to install XFree86 when compiling from raw
sources (not from a SRPM).  The suggestion is to install the
non-RPM version (or non-deb, etc.) in /usr/local/X11R6, leaving
the distribution-supplied version in /usr/X11R6.  That way,
you can switch between the versions at the user level just by
changing $PATH.  Oh, and you need to add /usr/local/X11R6/lib
to /etc/ld.so.conf and run ldconfig in order to get access to
the shared newer shared libraries.  That's how I put non-Redhat
4.2.0 in /usr/local/X11R6 while keeping the Redhat-RPM 4.1.0
in /usr/X11R6, and each user could choose which to use.

Good luck.

Robert Riches
