I've compiled the Linux kernel 2.4.18 and iptables 1.2.5 from source;
the kernel so that I can get decent performance compared to the 2.4.3
kernel, and iptables so that I can get my masquerading back.

So my next question is whether the XFree86-4.1.* RPMS from RedHat
are likely to work with the combination. (It did not work with the
kernel-2.4.3-21 kernel that RedHat compiled, and the kernel-2.4.9-?
kernel doesn't like my PC164 machine.)

As much as possible I want to stick with a canonical RedHat system
of RPMS so that I can worry about using my computer instead of managing
it. The XFree86-4.0.3-21 rpms work on my PCI ATI 3D Rage Pro 215GP,
so I will stand pat if there is any risk.

Incidentally, are there RPMS for iptables?
