There are a number of things that could be improved but one that has upset many potential Linux/Alpha users has been the difficulty of installing RedHat 7.1 on Milo only machines. I've seen comments like, upgrade to SRM and certainly on systems I have that can run SRM, I've moved to but we have to realize that there are lots of Milo only machines out there.

Now I know it's not too difficult for someone who knows what to do to build a new kernel for the installation process provided you have another working alpha system, but it's a bit chicken and egg for someone who has picked up an Alpha for a few dollars to play with, only to discover (probably after lots of time and effort) that they cannot install on their box.

I'm more than happy to test and contribute a new kernel and Milo setup for an XL366 and a UDB if anyone needs one. Perhaps we could setup a repository of suitable boot and root disks? We will also need to create suitable documentation to explain how to do the install.

