> > emulation so that you can latch into the onboard BIOS config
> > tools that the
> > like of SCSI cards tend to have. I doubt LinuxBIOS has that
> > ability though I'm
> > reasonably sure that some nutter will go out of their way to add
> > it. As for
> > SRM, I don't know too much about the internals of it or how much
> > BIOS emulation
> > would cost in terms of size for it to squeeze into onboard prom size.
> 
> Unfourtunetly, Linux kernel drivers for things like SCSI and others do
> expect
> the bios's to be run and have some set of default values. when that is not
> the case is usually not handled well. QL FC driver comes to mind. Mostly the
> EV6 SRMs only have BIOS emulation that is selectable. AS1200
> and I think AS800 are the exceptions. Even then it's limited to the devices
> SRM has drivers for, not what's simply present on the PCI bus (probably for
