On Tue, Mar 05, 2002 at 09:57:57AM +0100, Linus Gasser wrote:
> But I read that there 
> are some problems for non-i386 machines,

"Some problems" with 2.4.18 you refer to there are few lines, three or
four, which somehow got lost between 2.4.18rc4 and 2.4.18 and which
allow you to run Netscape from DU on your Linux/Alpha. :-)  You can patch
sources yourself (a patch is trivial) or you can use 2.4.18rc4 and change
EXTRAVERSION in the top Makefile.  Effects will be really the same.

If you want to look at details, and a small storm caused by this nasty
slip, then check archives of linux-kernel list.

> Anyway the -ac series seem to be a bit more stable.

This very much depends on _which_ kernel from that series you are
using.  It is not advisable to jump there without careful reading
release notes beforehand.  BTW - 2.4.18, or 2.4.18rc4 if you prefer,
looks pretty stable to me.

  Michal




