On Wed, Mar 06, 2002 at 06:59:37AM -0600, Carlos López wrote:
> 
>    Ext3, is supportted under redhat 7.1 for Alpha ??

Not for the original release, IIRC, but with updates yes.

> and, how can i install ??

Install, at minimum, kernel, e2fsprogs and modutils from updates and
read manpage for tune2fs; options '-j' and '-J' in particular.  Apply.
Edit your /etc/fstab to change file system type on filesystem you want
from ext2 to ext3.  If this does not include '/' (recommended for first
tries until you know that you got it right) then reboot and you are
done.   If you want ext3 on '/' as well then you need either a kernel
with ext3 support built-in (in an "official" kernel from updates this is
a module) or a proper initrd for that module to be loaded before '/' is
mounted.

Try first on a system when you can afford to botch things and you know
how to recover.

To back-off edit /etc/fstab again and reboot (but you have to be able to
get to fstab in the first place).  If you are switching to ext3, ext2
and ext3 again do not replay an old journal as you may get nasty
surprises.  Recreate it before the last step.

Messing with filesystems while in a multi-user mode is usually not
a good idea.

  Michal




