There appears to be a security vulnerability in the Netscape
browser supplied with RH7.1 for Alpha.  (I know, I really should
switch to Mozilla.  :-)

By happenstance, I pressed the mouse button 2 (middle) with the
cursor on an open area of a local page I had written.  This
vectored the browser window to IP address 211.185.192.66 (which
"whois" says is a school in Korea) with the name "Lee Kwan Hyung"
displayed on the page.  Being as the only interaction I have had
with Korean schools is in receiving and reporting spam, this was
a bit of a surprise.

A few months ago, a Swedish newspaper (aftonbladet.se) did
something very similar, and deleting ~/.netscape cured that
problem.  This time, however, that was not sufficient, implying
that the nasties have worked their way into root-owned files.
Yikes!!!

Any suggestions for tracking down and eliminating the infection
and/or preventing it from coming back?

Thanks.

Robert Riches
richesr1@inetarena.com




