	There was a very early Microsoft internal only
	64-bit port of Windows 2000 demonstrated at the
	June, 1998 PC Expo. It was running on an Alpha
	with a 64-bit version of SQL Server. I think that
	was the only time it was ever shown to the public.

	All development of 64-bit Windows was done on
	Alpha's until Intel got Microsoft a bunch of
	Itanic systems. I don't believe that any further
	development on Alpha's is being done.
	
	One of the nice things that was in the Win2k 32-bit
	Alpha version was more hardware support and FX!32
	was built in to the Windows kernel.

	It's all a moot point anyways.  Why folks want to
	try and run Alpha Windows2000 is beyond me. Especially
	when there are much faster x86 systems today.

								mike

