Thank you. I did have glibc-devel installed but it did not provide 
rquota.h. I went to rpmfind to doublecheck whether it was a mistake and 
it wasn't. However, after a nudge from another person from this list and 
noticing that mi i686 machine has rquota.h installed from two packages, 
I installed on the Alpha the second package (for the first one, 
glibc-devel, was already installed). The second package was 
compat-glibc. After I installed it, netatalk compiled like a champ, and 
now my MOSX machines can mount volumes from my Alpha through AppleTalk. 
Good ending!

