Should not need source to compile stuff,
can get asm functionality with

#pragma intrinsic (asm)

and maybe

#define __asm__ asm

see hints in 'c_asm.h' that comes with ccc

"most" gcc options are recognised by ccc,
don't need to change the makefiles use

CC=ccc make -e

however, if you want to try this I would NOT begin with 'X'
or the kernel, try something smaller,
just turn on all the warnings and read the log files :-)
Stephen Lewis

