On Thu, Mar 07, 2002 at 08:25:26AM -0700, Thursday AKA dr. john wrote:
> I think an open source software developer is in a similar position as a
> provider of public goods.  The more work you do, the more important it
> is and the better you do it ...  the MORE people will complain. The more
> complainers there are the more noticable becomes the small percentage
> who are truly nasty and vicious.   You almost never hear from the people
> who are happy and satisfied. =20
>=20
> Why is it like that?

Because many people are more likely to complain about issues then are
willing to prais/thank for good work. Often they appreciate someone
else work but don't tell the person so. Often one even doesn't notice=20
"good" work but rather not working products.

So taking your example, those who got a house were (mostly) pretty
happy but they simply would not consider going to you and telling you
"Thank you". I am sure if you went round and asked for some feeback
they would be glad to tell you how happy they are.

Greetings

