On Sun, Mar 10, 2002 at 08:47:03PM +0000, Tristan Hill wrote:
> 
> I'm trying to workout the SCSI configuration of a pws 433au.
> 
> It has a Qlogic ISP1020 controller (presumably on the riser).  Is
> this different to the "Qlogic 1040UW Ultra Wide SCSI PCI Adapter"
> mentionned in the User Information manual?

Check the SRM "show config" output, and it should give a "rev" of the
chip, though it will prolly still tell you it's a 1020. If the "rev"
is 5, it's actually a 1040B, capable of UW; if "rev" is 6, it's 1040C
also good for UW. Otherwise, if "rev" is 1 or 2, it's most likely good
only for fast/wide (20MB/sec tops).

Check the Qlogic website (www.qlogic.com) Products pages for details.

> The current disk is a quantum viking ii.  This has a jump to switch
> between SE mode and an auto switching between LVD and SE mode,
> currently set at the later.  Is this operating in LVD mode?  How
> could I find out?

IMHO, very unlikely if the QLogic is a 1020 or 1040.

--Jay++

