Note Alphas are feeble compared to it, even with the ccc compiler.
To be precise, it's 3.6x, 2.73x, and 2x the machine you tested on if
you believe this benchmark is a good measure of your machine's performance.

On my codes, the Athlon can't actually exceed the performance of an XP1000 
on any important codes. It can on some things but they represent less than 1%
of my compute load.

This benchmark is a very bad indicator of performance for anything I do
with Alphas. 

Given it has a clock advantage of 2.8x the XP1000, I think the XP1000 
can hold it's own. But then again, that Athlon cost less than $500 to build.


Wes

