Gentlemen,

I am trying to install XFree86-3.3.6 on a Jensen
Alpha XP machine after having compiled it full from sources
using the command: 
	make World
Compilation finished successfully with no errors.
However, after a: 
	make install
XFS hung the system during the bootup. Then, I had
to reboot to runlevel 1, single mode, in order fix it,
namely, to move the related xfs file from init.d
in order to return to runlevel 2 or 3.

Does anyone know what is causing this problem with
MAKE INSTALL and how to fix it ? MAKE INSTALL seems to be 
not working properly.

Thanks in advance,
    Luiz Emediato





