>> Hi!
>> 
>> My PWS 433 is running RedHat 6.2. Last fall I tried to upgrade kernel to
>> 2.2.19-6.2.12, but it failed. When I tried to boot the system after
>> installing the kernel, it displayed "length error" and then stopped. The
>> system is currently running with kernel 2.2.19-6.2.7 OK.
>> 
>> Does anyone know what is wrong?
>> 
   I have seen this problem on our 164LXs with kernel 2.2.16, so it isn't
   just a 2.2.19 issue.  I just upgraded to the recent RH 2.2.19 (with
   the zlib security fix) and saw this same issue again.  I don't know
   the correct answer, but an easy workaround is to point your bootloader
   to the *uncompressed* kernel vmlinux-2.2.x.x rather than to the 
   compressed kernel, which is usually the kernel that is booted.  We make
   a symbolic link "vmlinux" to the numbered vmlinux for convenience.




