On Fri, 15 Mar 2002, Rajiv Prasad wrote:

> Now, the question is how do I go about installing the new kernel and the
> new modutils?  In what sequence?  modutils first?  kernel first?  And
> where do I install modutils?  The README says by default it is installed
> in / -- that would blow away my old modutils, right?  Is it safe to do,
> or should I reconfigure to install modutils 2.4.14 in /usr/local?  If I
> do the latter, would the new kernel be able to find modutils in
> /usr/local and not use the old version of modutils (in /)?

You need a new modutils for a 2.4.x kernel, as their module layout is
different than 2.2.x kernels, so I would install that first.

Also, modutils kinda needs to be on /, so you don't get into wierd
situations of possibly trying to run modutils off a partition that isn't
mounted yet, and/or you have support for that filesystem as a module!

--
-- John E. Jasen (jjasen1@umbc.edu)
-- In theory, theory and practise are the same. In practise, they aren't.




