jjasen1@umbc.edu said:
>  Also, modutils kinda needs to be on /, so you don't get into wierd
> situations of possibly trying to run modutils off a partition that
> isn't mounted yet, and/or you have support for that filesystem as a
> module! 

That's quite unlikely, but the kernel will try to invoke /sbin/modprobe 
when it wants to autoload a module, so putting modutils elsewhere really 
isn't going to work very well.

If in doubt, make sure you build your new kernel with everything you need 
for normal operation built-in. Then you can play with modutils until you're 
happy with it.

--
dwmw2
