Hi folks:

Thanks for the replies.  It seems that what I'm trying to do has
potential pitfalls that I need to be aware of (thanks Michal for
pointing them out).

The system I'm trying to get a Linux installation with 2.4.x kernel is
new enough that I can afford to mess it up (short of destroying the disk
or user files in /home). :-)

I decided to take Michal's advice and try to put RH7.1 on this machine. 
So far, the attempt has been a total failure.  Here's what's in the
system:

SX164 533MHz 21164PC
384MB RAM (2x64 + 2x128 PC100 168pin DIMMs)
Toshiba CD-ROM (never had any problems with it, RH6.1 boots from it
okay)
2 IDE disks on primary IDE channel, both used by NT 4.0
1 UDMA 100 Seagate 60GB disk (slave on the same IDE channel as the
CD-ROM, where I have RH6.1 now)
Adaptec 2940UW with a zip drive, a scanner, and a CD-RW drive on it (all
work fine in RH6.1, as well as NT4.0)
Soundblaster 16 (Creative Vibra..., works fine)
US Robotics ISA voice/fax modem (works fine)
Matrox Millenium II 4MB PCI (no trouble)

Now to the troubles trying to install RH7.1:

1. none of the 2.2 MILOs work -- including the gatekeeper.dec.com
versions -- all stop at the MILO> prompt, won't even get input from the
keyboard!  The only working MILO I have is a 2.0.35 from the RH6.1 CD. 
If someone has a working 2.2 MILO for SX164, I'd like to get it to try.
2. so I tried making the boot disk (generic.img) and ramdisk
(ramdisk.img) from the RH7.1 CD, and boot with these (as RedHat says
"boot fd0:" at the MILO prompt choosing "linux" to boot the installer). 
MILO (2.0.35) goes into a booting loop.  I read somewhere how to fix
this particular problem, but now have forgotten -- any clues?
3. booting directly from the RH7.1 CDs doesn't work, as the
RELEASE-NOTES for RH7.0 warned about (no root filesystem on the 7.x
CDs??).

So, the only working installation I can get into is RH6.1.  I did not
try RH6.2 -- that may work, but as Michal points out, upgrading from 6.x
to something resembling 7.x will take a fair amount of work, even if I
were to be careful enough to sort out all inconsistencies (which I
doubt).

Any help is appreciated.

Rajiv

PS: Luke, how did you get RH7.0 on your MILO system?  Which MILO did you
use?  2.2 series?




