Hi,
I have another set of options you might give a try. They worked for me
on an XL300.
-Milo 2.0.35 (2.2.x won't work)
-take the Boot disk from the 7.0 CD
and surprise:
- take the Root disk from 7.1 CD
- have the 7.1 iso file copied (or ftp'd or whatever) to a disk
partition where you can access them from the initrd. This works, because
the 7.1 root disk can access iso files directly (they don't need to be
burned to a cd).
I did it this way, because my XL300 refuses to boot or install from cd.
Again: this worked for me. Give it a try & good luck.

Greetings,
Guus

