On Tue, 19 Mar 2002, JH wrote:

> The standard low density PC133, unbuffered(not registered), ECC will work
> fine.  The newer "high density" chips used on some of the newer modules are
> unsupported by the chipset and thus will not work.  Certain generic modules
> may also have compatibility problems.  Running PC133 at PC100 or PC66 will
> cause the memory latencies to be set at their theoretical minimims for SDRAM
> via the SPD.  The benefit of this is typically a jump in the integer
> performance (CAS2 vs CAS3).  Other more technical benefits exist as well.
>
> Jon




