When I shut down my LX164, the VGA display is sometimes scrambled. It
responds to SRM commands, though all I can detect is the pattern, not the
actual words. "test" works and produces the expected pattern of output. It
also boots, but the display never recovers. Loggin in from another
machine, I can start X, but when switch to the right console, nothing
happens (literally, nothing) -- the keyboard is not locked -- the lights
change when I push num or cap lock.

The reset button recycles the POST, but the console does not unscramble.  
Turning the power off for half a minute seems to work. I has always worked 
propertly after being off overnight.

My concern is that the video card may be going bad or that I may be
developing some other hardware failure. This is a 3 yr old machine with 
added memory and both a SCSI and an IDE HD. Video card is Matrox 
Millenium II, 4M.

This has occurred irregularly for about 10 days. The first time was after 
a storm of SCSI bus errors (I compiled a wrong driver).

Suggestions?

