in /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/doc, but nothing there seems to help me.

Just doing an rpm -Uvh says I need the following:
xinitrc >=3.13
Glide3 (do I really need this if I don't have a 3dfx card?)
kernel-drm
mkfontdir

I'm running the kernel-2.4.9-21 that I got from rawhide.  I notice there
is a kernel-2.4.9.-31HACK on rawhide.  Does this contain the
kernel-drm?  Do I need to compile my own kernel?   Isn't mkfontdir
supposed to come with xfree-4.2-xfs?  I installed it with --nodeps, but
it still says I don't have mkfontdir.

Please help.  I stupidly installed a couple of the 4.2 packages with
--nodeps, so now I have no X until I get this fixed.  When will I learn
:P

