On Fri, Mar 22, 2002 at 10:06:01AM -0700, nairnr@nairnconsult.hn.org wrote:
> 
> Hi all,
> 
> I have RH7.1 on my Alpha (AS 1000a 5/333) with a reasonably large root
> partition. Originally when I installed it it only gave me ext2 as a
> partition type. Is it possible to migrate this to a ext3 by ading a journal
> to it? I have had a few times where I had to reboot the machine and it took
> a while to do all the checking. I realize that in the fstab I can add a
> journal=inode or something like that and it will use it. Will the booting
> process have any difficulties with this? Has anyone else tried this?  

If you have the space (a few megs), and assuming you've updated all
the required tools (and the kernel) to a version that's ext3 capable,
all it should take is running /sbin/tune2fs -j <device>

Of course, you'll then need to change your fs type in your fstab to
ext3 and reboot (although there's probably a way around rebooting, I
just didn't feel like experimenting). But, yeah.. it can be
done.. I've done it with several of my machines already.

--
Ryan Schaefer
rysch@chaank.com




