I've been compelled by various events to change the prom on my PC164
from the ARC to SRM. It handles my IntraServer SCSI card just fine,
but I find that my ATI 3D RAGE PRO video card is no longer useable.
I guess it's because the BIOS emulator in the SRM console is not
good enough to boot the card.

I've shoved an S3 in there for now, but this has *got* to be temporary.
I do imaging, this is not good enough. I see a couple possibilities:

    1) Install both the S3 and the ATI card, and let the SRM do its
    boot stuff on that display, and run X on the ATI card. I presume
    that the Mach64 server can configure a virgin card.

    2) Similarly, maybe I can run the SRM (and possibly the kernel
    as well) out to a serial console, and start X at boot time to
    activate the ATI card.

    3) Find a decent PCI video card that is compatible with Linux,
    SRM, and the PC164.

    3b) Find a version of SRM that supports the ATI card. (I like
    this option the best.)


