Hi folks:

I finally got 7.1 installed on my SX164, thanks to all the wonderful help 
from you guys.  I had to use the 7.0 installation files (bootdisk and 
ramdisk).  The 7.0 installer would not recognize my burnt 7.1 CDs, nor the 
7.1 ISOs (if I used the 7.1 ramdisk along with 7.0 bootdisk).  I don't know 
why this happened (was it checking for 7.0 md5sums??), but then I pointed the 
installer to use ftp.redhat.com -- the 7.1 installation tree.  Thirty-four 
hours later (these cable modems are cool...) I had 7.1 installed.  Looking 
back, maybe I should have put the whole 7.1 installation tree on a local 
partition for the 7.0 installer to use.  Maybe next time...

I built and installed kernel 2.4.19-pre3 using stock 7.1 compilers/binutils, 
put it on a floppy and booted.  It worked.  So installed 2.4.19-pre3 in 
/boot, and am now booting directly from disk using milo 2.0.35 without any 
problems.  Need to rebuild thekernel with cool modules like usb support now...

Now, I have more questions:

1. there are a lot of update files for 7.1 (I downloaded all rpms, it is 
worth 301MB).  How do I figure out the inter-dependencies for these rpms?  Or 
is just a brute-force "rpm --force --install *.rpm" okay?  Don't want to mess 
up *this* installation.

2. I am a little unclear about the layout of /boot.  What do System.map and 
modules.info files do?  They are symlinks to System.map-2.4.3-12 and 
module.info-2.4.3-12.  Do I have to put System.map and module.info from my 
2.4.19-pre3 build in /boot, and modify the symlinks?  2.4.19-pre3 boots 
without these files.  So why are they there?  BTW, I could not find 
module.info in my 2.4.19-pre3 build tree.  Where is it?

3. dhcp:  while I was installing, the hostname was set to dhcp-102-6, and it 
is sticking even now.  When I was using RH6.1, I used to get hostname and 
domainname from dhcp.  Why not in 7.1:

[rajiv@dhcp-102-6 rajiv]$ hostname
dhcp-102-6
[rajiv@dhcp-102-6 rajiv]$ domainname
(none)

BTW, dhcpcd is not running.  Is that the default?  Do I need to run dhcpcd to 
get back the 6.1 behavior?

So far, I love 7.1 with KDE 2.x.  Konqueror is great, except that on some 
websites the fonts get totally messed up (too small/blocky) -- any idea why?

Thanks for the help again, and I do expect to have a lot more questions to 
throw out at you guys. ;-))

Cheers,
Rajiv




