> What exactly is the limitation in the SRM that restricts video card
> support? Is it that the BIOS emulator is not so good as the one in
> the ARC console?

It's which BIOS emulator the respective consoles where built with. Pre EV6
consoles stop at around x2.01 for BIOS emulation, That is enough to support
3dfx. You can see the version number when it turns on. In the case if the PC164
I'm unsure of the justification as to why they went different routes with the
emulators. I think the PC164 SRM (or is it the EB164?)uses the BIOS emulator
distributed with the EBSDK, It'll say so when the emulators shows its version
number at power on or 'init'.  I'm pretty sure that will support voodoos too. It
would have to since I remember using a voodoo3 in my UP1000 and when you are in
diagnostics  'that' piece of firmware (not SRM) uses the EBSDK's BIOS emulator.
That worked.

Peter
