> I noticed when starting the X Server that the screen looks like
> it is running the BIOS, before the server finally takes over. Does XFree86
> really include its own emulator, and can I use that to make it work?

voodoo@alphadriven.org said:
> You now have to deal with the logistics problem of not having a
> console until X starts. That is you have only one video output to your
> monitor and it's hooked up to the second video card.

Here's what I *just* got to work:

I left the S3 968 in, and I added the ATI card. Kudzu was nice enough
to discover and configure the card for me. I configured it (but did
not let it test) and continued on with boot.

Now I log it and type startx, then switch the monitor cable to
the ATI card, and I'm suddenly viewing more acceptable video. Kool!
I didn't set the BusID in the XF86Config file, it seems to reject
the S3 device when the Mach64 server is in use (no great surprise)
but I'll add it for completeness sake.

It's all a bit hackish, but frankly I only need the SRM console
(and the 968 card) when I'm booting, and that's pretty darn rare,
so I don't mind. At the very least, I've got something that works
well enough while I ponder more expensive options.

A variant of this plan might be to use the SERIAL port as an SRM
and kernel output path, but I don't have a terminal to hook up.
