Hi folks:

I decided to take Michal's advice -- again! -- :-) -- and stay away from "rpm 
--force" -- I'll just be selective upgrading (-Uvh) rpms that I really need 
to.  (Sorry Michal, with my every post I have a feeling I am pushing you 
closer to a heart attack! ;-)  Just to make it clear, you have been a *great* 
help so far!  Thanks!!)

The dhcp issue was resolved by setting "HOSTNAME=" in /etc/sysconfig/network, 
which had "HOSTNAME=dhcp-102-6".  /etc/hosts was messed up too for the 
loopback address -- I removed "dhcp-102-6" from that line, and now I get my 
fully qualified hostname just as it was in 6.1.

Here's another question: my "make modules_install" ends with:

cd /lib/modules/2.4.19-pre3; \
mkdir -p pcmcia; \
find kernel -path '*/pcmcia/*' -name '*.o' | xargs -i -r ln -sf ../{} pcmcia
if [ -r System.map ]; then /sbin/depmod -ae -F System.map  2.4.19-pre3; fi
depmod: *** Unresolved symbols in 
/lib/modules/2.4.19-pre3/kernel/drivers/ide/ide-probe-mod.o
depmod:         ide_xlate_1024_hook

Does not look quite right (incomplete to say the least, maybe more 
serious...) to me.  Did not have any problems with "make boot" and "make 
modules".  Any ideas?

Thanks for the help.

Rajiv




