On Sat, Mar 23, 2002 at 01:48:57PM -0800, Stephen Williams wrote:
> 
> steve@icarus.com said:
> > What of the Oxygen VX1 and ilk video cards? A bit more expensive, but
> > I remember seeing that name while browsing Compaq's alphaserver pages.

VX1 and ELSA (Permedia-2) do both work, at least at SRM level.

> Here's another guess: ATI Radeon 32MB PCI SDR

They don't work - black screen, no SRM.

Here's what I just tried, in PC164 with SRM v5.5-1; all the working
ones succeeded in getting to SRM without problems, but that doesn't
mean that XFree86 will run on all of them...

WORK
----
Matrox Millennium I (assume II as well)
ELSA Gloria Synergy (Permedia-2)
3DLabs Oxygen VX1 (Permedia-3)
Diamond Stealth III S540 (Savage4)
TGA/TGA2 :-)

Of the above, I'm not sure if the Savage4 will work under XFree86 on
a SPARSE box like PC164; the others, I'm pretty sure WILL...

I'd also assume that Permedia-2V based cards will also work, as all the
Permedia chipsets are handled by common code in the GLINT driver.

If I had to recommend anything, that you still stand a good chance of
finding (unlike the Millenniums), it would be the Permedia-2 based
cards. Most come with 8MB of memory, making 24-bit color easy, though
the RAMDAC is not fast enough to run deeper than 16-bits at 75Hz
refresh. Both the VX1 and Savage4 are faster and have more memory
and higherr refresh rates, but are apt to be more expensive.


DO NOT WORK
-----------
3DFx Banshee (precursor to Voodoo3)
ATI Rage 128
ATI Radeon
nVidia TNT2

Good luck.

--Jay++

