Quoting Michal Jaegermann <michal@ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca>:

> On Mon, Mar 25, 2002 at 01:45:44PM +0100, Heid Oliver wrote:
> 
> > I got the impression during recent power failures on two machines
> > (2.4.19-pre kernels, one
> > with a qlogic, one with a symbios controller) that fsck from the
> RH7.1
> > update e2fsprogs
> > package (e2fsprogs-1.23 AFAIR) destroyed the filesystems. I now use
> the
> > original
> > e2fsprogs-1.19-5 again, and had no problems so far.
> 
> To be sure package from current updates to 7.1 is
> e2fsprogs-1.26-1.71.alpha.rpm
> If it has some hidden problems or not I do not know.  Did you report
> your findings on bugzilla?
> 
> If somebody plans to work with ext3 then e2fsprogs-1.19 it is not
> enough.
> 
>    Michal

    Hi everyone,

I can confirm that there is a problem with e2fsprogs from RH7.1 updates.

I get a power failure. e2fsck couldn't fix 20 GB partitions formatted in ext3
but mounted for now in ext2 (it ends up with a segfault).

I decided to delete and recreate these partitions. Now mke2fs complains with
this error when I try format with the options -c and/or -j :

--
mke2fs: Attempt to write block from filesystem resulted in short write zeroing
block xxxxxx at end of filesystem
----
is xxxxxx relevant to you ?

I tried with partition size of 10 and 20 GB.

My kernel is 2.4.17. My box is based on a AlphaPC 164LX. My harddrive is an IBM
IDE 60 GB drive.

Thanks in advance for any help.

Sincerely yours, Mathieu.

--
Mathieu MILLET
