Hi guys,

A while back I bought a UP1100 motherboard off Ebay.com for the sum of
$US600 - lucky me ;-)

I asked the seller to send it to me about a month ago I waited a couple of
weeks for it arrive to me - in the UK via USPS. However it didn't arrive so
I contacted the seller and queried him and he said he hadn't sent it because
I hadn't told him how I wanted it to be dealt with by customs. Anyway I
asked him to resend it. It still hasn't arrived after 3 weeks. I've bought
items from ebay before and they usually arrive within a couple of days.

 So is this normal? Should I be prepared to wait a little longer. I've
contacted the seller since and now he doesn't reply to my emails. I'd have
thought that if this is a fraud that a UP1100 would be an odd item to pick
because they are relatively rare, I'd have thought that if someone was going
to pull a fast one that more likely deal with a more common item such as a
Pentium motherboard. The seller has feedback with a couple of negative
replies but in general nothing out of the ordinary.

If this is fraud does anyone know what sort of action I could take?

Kind regards,

Peter Watkinson
peterw@u.genie.co.uk




