So again - was this reported on bugzilla?

On http://e2fsprogs.sourceforge.net/ from March 8th there is a release
1.27 of e2fsprogs made, among other things, to fix bugs which affect
mips and Alpha.  I do not know if these fixes were incorporated in the
latest version from updates.

> --
> mke2fs: Attempt to write block from filesystem resulted in short write zeroing
> block xxxxxx at end of filesystem
> ----
> is xxxxxx relevant to you ?

This sounds like a problem with an access to the last block if a number
of blocks on a disk is odd.  That likely would be a kernel fault and not
a trouble with mke2fs.

