On Tue, Mar 26, 2002 at 09:55:43AM -0800, Stephen Williams wrote:
> 
> 0) Forget ARC and MILO. Hopeless. The kernels on the cdrom are not
>    compatible with milo.

As documented in release notes.  If you want to use milo you
have to compile your own kernel with CONFIG_ALPHA_LEGACY_START_ADDRESS
set to 'y'.  If you will do that then a resulting kernel does not
boot on "Wildfire" class machines, I am told.

> 1) If the disk you are installing on previously had DOS style
>    partitions and not BSD partitions, then fdisk will *not* automatically
>    go to BSD mode. You have to do this yourself.

In bugzilla for some time already.

> 
> 2) Even if you make a blank partition table and let disk druid do
>    partitioning, it will not properly account for aboot or srm
>    requirements, in spite of the claims in the documentation.

Ditto.

> After Installation:
> 
> 1) kernel-2.4.3-12 is unstable.

That one you got on CD should not even boot with milo.  If you are using
SRM then there are updates.

> 2) kernel-2.4.9-anything will not even boot.

See number 0.

  Michal




