I pulled open a (btw be carefull when you disassemble these) RZ28C-VW with SN:
CX61612132. This is a "tan" SBB and has a 68 pin internal connector. You you may
be able to do is get a BOM (bill of materials) from compaq support. I remember
Kurt has the list for the drives you have with SCA connectors. Ironicly "I" have
a bunch of SBB's with 68 pin internal connecters of which I want to upgrade to
SCA. The part is about $75, Though for that price you may be better off going to
pricewatch and buying NEW 9GB SCA disks for around $100. Stick to seagates and
quantums if you go that route.

