That is if CPQ will sell you the parts =/. I was trying to completely
retrofit the SBB's to the internal SCA connector from the 50 pin SCSI
narrow that they came with. The flexi circut board that the LEDs are
mounted to that display drive status have a different connector on the end
for the SCA vs. std connector. They wouldn't sell me that part number when
I called them as remaining stock was reserved for waranty replacement =/.
So the SBB -> SCA adapters may have gone the same route now. But yes, they
were $75 a piece + shipping (shipping was cheap though).

If you're going to use the 50 pin -> SBB back plates, they are tailored
for specific drives that have specific spacing between the power connector
and the SCSI connector. IIRC DEC/CPQ used seagate and quantum drives
(which they'd change the firmware on the them to reflect a DEC part #).
The SBB's that I have had Seagate 4.3G drives in them.

if you've got the SCA's you can plop just about anything in the SBBs
(slimline or 1/2 height 3 1/2") that has an SCA connector. If you still
have foam on the top panel of the SBB, 1/2 heights are a bit of a squeeze
