-Thinks if you've got SCA connectors go with the SCA drives. If they're
not SCA, you have to set the IDs on each drive indivitually. With SCA, the
SBB backplane will set them automatically (starting from 0 with the top
slot) at least on the DigitalServer 5300 / AS1200. That's the only thing I
own that actually uses these overpriced things =) and thus the only thing
I have had experience with. Something like an AS2100 may not due to its
age.


