aziegenfus@mindspring.com said:
> I'm a little confused here; maybe it's just cuz I don't know much
> about all this. I have a PC 164LX and I have RH 7.1 working fine with
> MILO. I installed it right off the CD, and things worked fine from
> there. 

ARC console is different from AlphaBIOS console.

Also, under certain limited conditions, certain MILOs are able
to boot the RedHat 7.1 kernels. In fact, before this mishap I was
able to boot a 2.4.3-12 kernel from a 2.0 based milo (though none
of the milos on the 7.1 disks, a well known problem) so long as no
parameters were required.

The fatal glitch in my case was that there was no way to pass
the root= option that was required to get the kernel on the install
CD to find the install root. (It found my /dev/sda2 root instead).
So the milos on the install disk wouldn't run at all, and the milo
I was able to scratch together from my old installation was not
able to pass the root= parameter to the kernel on the cdrom.

And thus, no way to run the install.


aziegenfus@mindspring.com said:
> The only thing is I can't figure out how to get it to boot right off
> my hard drive since AlphaBios doesn't seem to recognize my second hard
> drive (on the second IDE connector.)

Put a small FAT partition on your first partition to carry the milo
that you boot. Maybe?

