On Thu, Mar 28, 2002 at 09:29:18AM -0700, Chris Price wrote:
> 
> Everything goes OK until somewhere around 'transferring install image',
> 'preparing to install', or when the first package gets installed. At
> this point, the system completely 
> locks up; no mouse, or keyboard input is recognized
> 
> 	Any ideas?

Try installing in 'text' mode.  Seems to be less prone to stupid
hardware tricks.

If you are booting from CD then do that with '-fl i' instead of '-fl 0'
and 'l' at aboot prompt will show you a list of predefined boot lines.
Maybe the one with "text" is already there.  If not then type "b",
follow with all content of a line you were using and append " text" to
it (without quotes).

Also boot/ramdisk pair of floppies from 7.0 should work with 7.1 CDs.
In some hardware/firmware situations some apparently had better luck
with these.

  Michal




