On Thu, Mar 28, 2002 at 09:29:18AM -0700, Chris Price wrote:
> 
> 	Got my PC164 mobo working. Thnx to all who replied. For those who
> might care, the culprit was bent cpu pins.

Not an easy thing to detect without removing it... ;-}

> 	From SRM, I can boot the redhat 7.1 alpha cdrom and start the install
> program. 
> 	
> 	boot dqa1 -fl 0
> 
> Everything goes OK until somewhere around 'transferring install image',
> 'preparing to install', or when the first package gets installed. At
> this point, the system completely 
> locks up; no mouse, or keyboard input is recognized
> 
> 	Any ideas?

Yes; install RH 7.0 and then upgrade to 7.1 but keep using the 7.0
kernel (which is based on 2.2).

Or perhaps try booting the 7.0 kernel from floppy, and use the 7.1
RAMdisk floppy and see if it works.

Reason: RH 7.1 2.4.3-based kernel is broken on PC164 when booted from
SRM console. In fact, all 2.4.x kernels until 2.4.11 (IIRC) were broken
on PC164 booted from SRM (but are OK if booted from MILO).

Good luck.

