I have almost exactly the same configuration you have. SCSI
cdrom, instead of IDE.

cprice@its.to said:
> Everything goes OK until somewhere around 'transferring install
> image', 'preparing to install', or when the first package gets
> installed. At this point, the system completely  locks up; no mouse,
> or keyboard input is recognized

Sounds a little like the PC164/srm-is-unstable-with-2.4.3 problem.
Try installing 7.0 then upgrading. The 7.0 distro includes a 2.2
kernel that is more stable for your configuration. Or try to use
a boot/ramdisk floppy set from the 7.0 install to run the 7.1 install,
for the same reason.

I installed 7.1 on almost exactly the configuration you have, but
had to immediately install a 2.4.18 kernel to get it stabilized.
Fortunately, the 2.4.18 kernel compiles nicely, since none of the
RedHat supplied kernels is reliable on PC164/srm.

7.1 works great once you get past the bundled kernel.

Hint: Do not update XFree86 from the errata.
