Dear Stephen,

The 433au will be just fine as-izz.   SRM is the best if you've got it,
if you have your boot device and boot flags set, all you have to do is
type "boot" when the blue screen comes up.

There have been a lot of install problems in this class machine, my own
included, which trace back to it's having a tough time reading from the
CDrom drive.  Ultimate cause, unknown.  In my case i changed CD drives
and things went fine.

If you are lucky you have a decent video card.  If not, you have
alternatives provided you are only running Linux.

I like RedHat, mostly 'cause you can buy the boxed set of RedHat 7.1
plus a bunch of extras through Compaq for $29.95

good luck

jn




