For a 164LX you want to choose the CMD64X (not the CMD640) driver.
In "make xconfig" the options I use for my LX under "IDE ATA and ATAPI block
devices" are:

Enhanced IDE disk/tape/floppy support  Y (or M if your using modules)
Include IDE/ATA-2 disk support         Y (or M)
Use Multi Mode by default              Y
Generic PCI chipset support            Y
Generic PCI DMA support                Y
Use PCI DMA by default when available  Y
CMD64X chipset support                 Y

Once you've booted with the new kernel, you can tweak a bit more with the
hdparm command.  For example, before I mount the partitions, I have a
"hdparm -c 3 /dev/hda" command run.  Be careful with some of the hdparm
options.  The documentation is not kidding about some being dangerous.

Alan

