I added an IBM 73LZX 18.1G SCSI drive as a 2d drive to an LX-164. Any
partition larger than about 4G returned "short write" error when making
the e2fs. 4G partitions work. Single partition fails. The first drive is
an IBM 4.5 G that is supposed to be internally terminated (labels say
nothing).  The cable has no terminator (and does not extend beyond this
older drive).

No BSD labels (tried and undid it). Either fdisk or sfdisk (shudder)  
produce the same results.

This is RH 7.1, up to date, stock kernel 2.4.18 (actually patched with
19-pre4, then reversed).

Any hints appreciated.

