Hi folks:

I am running kernel 2.4.19-pre4 on an SX164 under RH7.1.  ipchains was 
configured during the install to "medium" security.  I want to enable 
talk/ntalk using xinetd, but only locally.  Here is the relevant 
configuration:

1. /etc/services contains:
talk            517/udp
ntalk           518/udp

2. /etc/xinetd.conf contains the following lines:
defaults
{
        instances               = 60
        log_type                = SYSLOG authpriv
        log_on_success          = HOST PID
        log_on_failure          = HOST
        cps                     = 25 30
        enabled                 = talk
        only_from               = localhost
}

includedir /etc/xinetd.d

3. /etc/xinetd.d/talk contains:
service talk
{
        disable                 = no
        socket_type             = dgram
        wait                    = no
        user                    = nobody
        group                   = tty
        server                  = /usr/sbin/in.talkd
}

4. /etc/sysconfig/ipchains contains:
-A input -p udp --dport talk -j ACCEPT

After making changes to config files, I restarted ipchains and xinetd.  No 
errors were reported.  However, if I try to use talk, it complains:

[rajiv@ts46-01-qdr1065 rajiv]$ talk rajiv
talk: ntalk/udp: service is not registered.

What am I missing?  Do I need to somehow register ntalk/udp?  Isn't an entry 
in /etc/services enough?

Thanks for any pointers.

Rajiv




